<title>JAPAN: Yamaichi shares extend losses after raid.</title>
<headline>Yamaichi shares extend losses after raid.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Yamaichi Securities Co Ltd extended losses on Thursday morning, following Wednesday's raid on the brokerage house by Tokyo prosecutors, brokers said.</p>
<p>By 0047 GMT, the shares had declined 21 yen to 259 yen, hitting a new low for this calendar year. It was below the previous day's low of 275 yen.  </p>
<p>&quot;We're worried about a negative effect on the market from investors deciding to suspend business with Yamaichi and the possibility of the Finance Ministry imposing penalties on Yamaichi, which is not as financially strong as Nomura,&quot; said a trader at a foreign securities house.</p>
</text>
